sments: [{knowledge_id, decision: used|considered|rejected|unresolved, rationale, transformed_mechanism, variant_names, nearest_work_difference, falsifier}]. Cover retrieved industry cards; identify the concrete changed mechanism for used cards. This is provenance, not causal proof.\",\n      \"reflection\": \"Review the latest knowledge-usage.json alongside outcomes; distinguish declared use, executed changes, mechanism evidence and unresolved attribution.\"\n    },\n    \"latest_knowledge_usage\": {\n      \"revision\": \"knowledge-access-v3\",\n      \"retrieved_ids\": [\n        \"unirank-method-infnet\",\n        \"unirank-method-ssr\",\n        \"paper:infnet\",\n        \"paper:tokenformer\"\n      ],\n      \"assessments\": [\n        {\n          \"knowledge_id\": \"unirank-method-infnet\",\n          \"decision\": \"considered\",\n          \"rationale\": \"Prior declared use produced executed task-score retrieval arms, but feedback-aware task routing did not improve click. This is mixed local evidence, not a confirmation of INFNet or a causal estimate of external knowledge value. Full token/hub replacement would confound the immediate selector backward-flow question.\",\n          \"transformed_mechanism\": \"No new hub or token component adopted; prior task-score rows are retained while a separate gradient-routing adaptation is tested.\",\n          \"variant_names\": [\n            \"primary_feedback\",\n            \"primary_item\",\n            \"joint_feedback\",\n            \"joint_item\"\n          ],\n          \"nearest_work_difference\": \"Single local-activation pooling stage with selectively blocked backward paths versus stacked task/proxy token interactions and gated broadcasts. Original v1 text and pinned benchmark forward code checked separately.\",\n          \"falsifier\": \"If the controlled backward intervention fails, do not credit INFNet-inspired task scoring for a nonexistent rescue; consider a separately controlled token/hub architecture only if new evidence justifies it.\",\n          \"source_refs\": [\n            \"unirank-benchmark-v2\",\n            \"unirank-code:INFNet\",\n            \"paper:infnet\"\n          ],\n          \"executed_refs\": [\n            {\n              \"trial_id\": \"g3-r0001-primary_feedback\",\n              \"source_sha256\": \"326619aa529dc14fc88372ab0b6bf7970ee8f253bb2c755e783ce080db429ebf\",\n              \"status\": \"success\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"trial_id\": \"g3-r0001-primary_item\",\n              \"source_sha256\": \"374482a0c33ac823d8b2a163fc3474b3bd65a6fdd605e2e56c4b64df1073f00b\",\n              \"status\": \"success\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"trial_id\": \"g3-r0001-joint_feedback\",\n              \"source_sha256\": \"4798255718c730c0b5fc2b02ec27078e7f8ae33adb9b98c85fadc6ea7639f519\",\n              \"status\": \"success\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"trial_id\": \"g3-r0001-joint_item\",\n              \"source_sha256\": \"9881103bbab989ce7239d3f1024a5a22320b8114f659d9040c9ffb9d17b6cec6\",\n              \"status\": \"success\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"evidence_class\": \"agent-declared usage; not mechanism confirmation\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"knowledge_id\": \"unirank-method-ssr\",\n          \"decision\": \"considered\",\n          \"rationale\": \"Activation sparsity after pooling is an alternative explanation/remedy for interference, but no local activation-interference evidence exists. The previous round deferred this intervention and the new AUC tradeoff still does not isolate it.\",\n          \"transformed_mechanism\": \"None adopted; no competitive sparse filter or multi-view fusion added.\",\n          \"variant_names\": [],\n          \"nearest_work_difference\": \"Candidate changes direct auxiliary gradient access to the selector rather than sparsifying forward activations after pooling. Original SSR paper is unaudited; card provenan